<circle cx="1179.6" cy="1400.0" r="10.2" class="hidden"/>
</g>
<text x="1080.0" y="1253.6" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">19.72 sq outer edge (lip tier, rounded R2.0)</text>
<line x1="1134.0" y1="1263.2" x2="1158.0" y2="1284.8" class="lead"/>
<text x="943.2" y="1320.8" text-anchor="end" font-size="11">wall 1.4</text>
<line x1="946.8" y1="1324.4" x2="972.0" y2="1332.8" class="lead"/>
<text x="943.2" y="1346.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="11">screw boss Ø4.6,</text>
<text x="943.2" y="1361.6" text-anchor="end" font-size="11">M2 pilot Ø1.7 × 5.0 deep</text>
<text x="943.2" y="1377.2" text-anchor="end" font-size="10">at (−8.3, 0) — inner flat for ESP32</text>
<line x1="946.8" y1="1353.2" x2="964.8" y2="1390.4" class="lead"/>
<text x="1216.8" y="1316.0" text-anchor="start" font-size="11">cavity 16.8 sq × 3.0 deep</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1331.6" text-anchor="start" font-size="10">(fits ESP32-C3-MINI-1, 16.6 long)</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1352.0" text-anchor="start" font-size="11">upper cavity 15.7 sq,</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1367.6" text-anchor="start" font-size="10">z 3.0 → 5.64 (dashed)</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1392.8" text-anchor="start" font-size="11">sensor c'bore Ø14.2 (dashed)</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1408.4" text-anchor="start" font-size="10">window Ø12.4 in top plate (dashed)</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1433.6" text-anchor="start" font-size="11">second boss at (+8.3, 0)</text>
<line x1="1213.2" y1="1430.0" x2="1192.8" y2="1412.0" class="lead"/>
<text x="943.2" y="1450.4" text-anchor="end" font-size="11">flat rim = PCB seating</text>
<text x="943.2" y="1466.0" text-anchor="end" font-size="11">face (back plane, z=0)</text>
<line x1="946.8" y1="1455.2" x2="973.2" y2="1436.0" class="lead"/>
<text x="1216.8" y="1476.8" text-anchor="start" font-size="11">arm: 5.18 wide, 3.0 thick,</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1492.4" text-anchor="start" font-size="10">flush with this back plane,</text>
<text x="1216.8" y="1508.0" text-anchor="start" font-size="10">tip at 30.4 diagonal</text>
<line x1="1213.2" y1="1481.6" x2="1204.8" y2="1512.8" class="lead"/>
<text x="1080.0" y="1548.8" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11">NO alignment posts — the two M2 screws at (+-8.3, 0) locate the PCB</text>
<text x="900" y="120" font-size="15" class="t2">NOTES</text>
<text x="900" y="142" font-size="13" class="t2">1. Measured 4.20 lip INCLUDES the 1.2 PCB edge -> plastic lip = 3.0</text>
<text x="900" y="164" font-size="13" class="t2">    (= arm, flush). Housing alone 7.24 tall; assembled with PCB 8.44.</text>
<text x="900" y="186" font-size="13" class="t2">    arm 5.18 wide; arm tip to opposite corner diagonal 30.4.</text>
<text x="900" y="208" font-size="13" class="t2">2. Corners rounded (R2.0 est) — no sharp turns, per NuPhy design.</text>
<text x="900" y="230" font-size="13" class="t2">3. Pad positions/pitch photo-derived — verify before PCB fab.</text>
<text x="900" y="252" font-size="13" class="t2">4. M2 = 2 mm-thread machine screw. Arm screw is countersunk M2;</text>
<text x="900" y="274" font-size="13" class="t2">    the two PCB screws are small M2 self-tappers into the housing.</text>
<text x="900" y="296" font-size="13" class="t2">5. Power: J11-1/2/3 = VBAT (tie together) -> 3.3 V LDO on module;</text>
<text x="900" y="318" font-size="13" class="t2">    J4-5 = GND. No keyboard data lines used (module is BLE).</text>
<text x="900" y="340" font-size="13" class="t2">6. PCB (~19.0 sq shown) screws onto the housing back; pads face out.</text>
</svg>